  "slug": "learning-body-interaction-fa56",
  "summary": "Three preprints on 18 Nov 2026 pair flow matching, Schrödinger bridges and diffusion rendering to model cell dynamics beyond fixed-population transport.",
  "synthesis": "The shared thread is generative modeling of how single-cell states evolve over time. Elysium is a simulation-free solver for unbalanced Schrödinger bridges that jointly learns state transitions and mass change. HORIZON applies flow matching to spatiotemporal cell dynamics from spatial transcriptomics and removes rigid frame motion. MitoWorld is a stochastic world model that generates future single-cell images under gene knockdown, combining latent dynamics, a division hazard, and diffusion rendering. What is new is the explicit handling of quantities that standard transport formulations tend to omit: mass change, division, and perturbation response. The works differ in modality, with expression, spatial transcriptomics, and images, so the common element is the generative dynamics framing rather than a shared data type. ST-FateFlow from the previous synthesis is not among the current items and is not carried forward.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-25"
}
